## 7. Model Validation Checklist

### Backtesting Protocol

**Phase 1: Historical Accuracy** (Last 30 Days)
- [ ] Run model on completed games
- [ ] Compare projections to actual results
- [ ] Calculate RMSE for each stat category:
  - Points: Target < 4.5
  - Rebounds: Target < 2.0
  - Assists: Target < 1.8
  - 3PM: Target < 1.0

**Phase 2: Betting Performance** (Next 2 Weeks)
- [ ] Track all recommended bets
- [ ] Measure win rate (target >54% at -110)
- [ ] Calculate ROI (target >5%)
- [ ] Track CLV on every bet (target >70% positive CLV)

**Phase 3: Feature Importance Analysis**
- [ ] Run SHAP analysis on our model
- [ ] Compare feature weights to Nature study findings
- [ ] Adjust weights if necessary
- [ ] Document changes in version control

### Red Flags to Monitor

**Model Drift Indicators**:
- Win rate drops below 50% for 20+ bets
- CLV consistently negative (lines moving against us)
- RMSE increases by >20% from baseline
- Specific stat category consistently overperforming/underperforming

**When to Recalibrate**:
- After major rule changes (mid-season adjustments)
- After All-Star break (pace/effort changes)
- When new referee trends emerge
- After significant injuries to key players

